Eden leak, performance, thermal & FPS limit patch v8
Base: eden-emulator/mirror master 6647b49cc (2026-11-15). Apply with: git apply eden-leak-perf-thermal-fpslimit-v8.patch
Contains v5, v6 and v7, plus the FPS limit below.

FPS limit (new in v8)
  * New setting "fps_limit" (Off / 20 / 30 / 60), per-game capable and changeable in-game from the
    quick settings sheet and in Settings > Graphics. It stretches the emulated display composition
    period (core/hle/service/vi/conductor.cpp), so the game gets fewer frame slots and really does
    less CPU/GPU work; the ADPF target follows. Fixed-timestep games run in slow motion when capped
    below their native rate. Android strings in English and Indonesian, Qt translations added.

Thermal (new in v7) - aims to keep the frame rate and cut wasted power
  * common/adpf.cpp - thermal guard. Uses AThermal_getThermalHeadroom (Android 11+, polled once a
    second) and the real per-frame load from v6. When frames are on time with plenty of slack
    (load EMA < 50%, or < 70% once the device is warm, headroom >= 0.80), the render ADPF session
    is put into power-efficiency mode (Android 15+). Any late frame leaves that mode immediately.
    Exposes IsThermallyConstrained() (headroom >= 0.95).
  * vk_turbo_mode.cpp - "Force maximum clocks" releases the GPU turbo request while the device is
    about to throttle and re-arms it once it has cooled down.
  * vk_scheduler.h - frame pacing (30/60/90/120 target modes) slept until ~1 ms before the frame
    and then spun on yield(), keeping a big core at 100% every frame. Linux/Android now use one
    absolute CLOCK_MONOTONIC sleep (sub-100 us accuracy). Other platforms keep the old path.
  * emu_window.cpp - the first surface frame-rate hint may switch the display mode non-seamlessly
    (while the game boots), so 120/144 Hz panels actually drop to 60 Hz for 60 fps games. Later
    hints stay seamless-only, so gameplay is never interrupted.

v6: ADPF reports real work time, turbo only while submitting, log rate limiting, cached GPU
probes, probe Surface release, input/netplay JNI leaks, VFS cache pruning.

Build note: -PYUZU_ANDROID_ARGS="-DYUZU_DOWNLOAD_ANDROID_VVL=OFF" drops the 24 MB validation layer.

